<report>
<title>Two sample Smirnov test for distribution difference</title>
<line></line>
<line>X sample: <in>x</in></line>
<line>Y sample: <in>y</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>Two sided test:</line>
<line>D = <inu>d</inu></line>
<line><pval><inp>p</inp></pval></line>
<line></line>
<line>One sided test (suspecting <in>sample_1</in> shifted left of <in>sample_2</in>):</line>
<line>D = <inu>d_l</inu></line>
<line><pval><inp>p_l</inp></pval></line>
<line></line>
<line>One sided test (suspecting <in>sample_1</in> shifted right of <in>sample_2</in>):</line>
<line>D = <inu>d_r</inu></line>
<line><pval><inp>p_r</inp></pval></line>
</report>
